  "id": "maternal-attitudes",
  "term": "maternal attitudes",
  "definition": "Maternal attitudes are a mother’s views or orientations about parenting and infant development, such as favoring more relational or more autonomous ways of raising a child. In this context, they are treated as beliefs that may shape, but do not always accurately predict, an infant’s day-to-day early environment.",
